{% extends '@EasyAdmin/layout.html.twig' %}
{#
  Base template for every redesigned NON-LIST admin page (dashboard, competitions,
  the three pool pages, league overview, locations).

  WHY THIS EXISTS. The shell's layout reproduces EasyAdmin's STOCK content_header_wrapper
  verbatim and on purpose — see its own note at bundles/EasyAdminBundle/layout.html.twig:126.
  Blanking that block broke every page that had NOT been redesigned, stripping their title
  and page-actions, so the default has to stay the real thing and pages that want the new
  strip override it themselves. That is what this file does, and it is the same pair of
  blocks the shipped list pages override (crud/bmc_index.html.twig:17,74).

  (The handoff's README explains this the other way round — that the layout puts the strip
  inside `content` and that overriding `content` is why the tool pages lost their headers.
  It does not: they look stock because nothing has migrated them yet. The conclusion is
  right even though the reason given for it is not.)

  So: override `content_header_wrapper` and `main`, via the bmc_* blocks below. Never
  override `content` in a child — that would swallow the strip for real.

  Variables (pass from the controller's render()):
    bmcGroup   crumb group, e.g. 'Config'            → "ADMIN › CONFIG"
    bmcTitle   page title (defaults to the selected menu label)
    bmcDomain  default card domain for the page: club | match | people
    bmc_page   OPTIONAL — only if <main data-bmc-page> comes out empty (see README §2.3)
#}

{% block content_header_wrapper %}
    <header class="bmc-strip">
        <div class="bmc-strip__titles">
            <span class="bmc-crumb">ADMIN › {{ bmcGroup|default('')|upper }}</span>
            <div class="bmc-title-row">
                <h1 class="bmc-title">{% block bmc_title %}{{ bmcTitle|default('')|upper }}{% endblock %}</h1>
                <button type="button" class="bmc-iconbtn bmc-iconbtn--sm bmc-pin" aria-pressed="false" title="Pin to sidebar">
                    <i data-lucide="pin" width="16" height="16"></i>
                </button>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="bmc-strip__right">
            {% block bmc_strip_right %}{% endblock %}
        </div>
    </header>
{% endblock %}

{% block main %}
    <div class="bmc-page{% block bmc_page_class %}{% endblock %}">
        {% block bmc_body %}{% endblock %}
    </div>
    {{ include('admin/_bmc_dialog.html.twig') }}
{% endblock %}
